  "_doc": "Verb allow-list for the verbless_sentence lint (2026-07-29 QA review: 'no sentence without a verb — this is what catches fragments programmatically'). `base` forms are expanded to +s/+es/+ed/+ing (with e-drop and consonant doubling) at module load; `forms` holds auxiliaries, copulas, modals, and irregular past/participle forms verbatim. The list skews toward picture-book register on purpose — it exists to prove a sentence HAS a verb, not to police which verb. Incomplete by design, which is why the lint is SOFT: a rare verb must not hard-bounce a good book.",
